    <briefdescription>
<para>io_uring-based async TCP server for low-latency, high-throughput I/O. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Uses <computeroutput>IORING_SETUP_SQPOLL</computeroutput> so that the kernel polls the submission queue without requiring <computeroutput>io_uring_enter()</computeroutput> on the hot path. In steady state, all accept/recv/send operations complete with zero syscalls on the application side.</para>
<para>Operations batched per io_uring ring:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>IORING_OP_ACCEPT</computeroutput> — non-blocking accept loop</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>IORING_OP_RECV</computeroutput> — per-connection read</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>IORING_OP_SEND</computeroutput> — per-connection write (zero-copy via fixed buffers)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Guarded by <computeroutput>THEMIS_ENABLE_IO_URING</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>__linux__</computeroutput>. On other platforms (or when the build flag is absent) <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_io_uring_server_1ac162240ef8b8ad4722e9f9d81e7f9aa2" kindref="member">start()</ref></computeroutput> returns false.</para>
<para>Performance characteristics:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Latency: 10–50 µs round-trip</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Throughput: up to 10 Gbps</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>CPU model: SQ polling thread in kernel; application threads can sleep </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
